{
  "requirement": "Return a snapshot of the observations collected so far. Later reads continue to contribute to this execution.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D> {\n    pub fn dependencies(&self) -> Vec<Dependency<D::NodeId, D::EdgeLabel>>;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.dependencies` has two obligations. It must return a snapshot of the observations collected so far. Later reads must continue to contribute to the same execution.\n\nThe marked test `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` covers both:\n- **Nothing collected yet:** `inspection.dependencies().is_empty()` is asserted right after `ValidationContext::new`, before any tracked read.\n- **Snapshot of what was collected so far:** after `read(&1)` returns \"before\", `earlier = inspection.dependencies()` is taken. The node content is then changed to \"after\" and read again. `assert_eq!(earlier, [Dependency::Node(1, fp(\"before\"))])` shows the returned value is an independent snapshot. The later read did not alter it.\n- **Later reads keep contributing:** the later `read(&1)` (now \"after\") shows up in the next call. `inspection.dependencies()` equals `[Node(1, before), Node(1, after)]`. A fresh call after the failed `read(&2)` also reflects the earlier reads, so collection continued.\n- **Same collection reaches the record:** `finish` produces a record whose `dependencies` equal the same two entries. This checks that the snapshot reflects the execution's actual collection.\n\nThe assertions are exact and ordered, so a snapshot that stops updating, aliases the live state, or drops or duplicates entries would fail. The other supplied test, `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]`, covers the public export inventory and is not relevant to the behavior of `dependencies`. No marking or assertion gap remains for this requirement, and there are no fixme acknowledgments.",
